# Copy to `.env` in this directory (`.env` is gitignored — never commit it).
# Fill in values locally. Do not paste real secrets into issues or chat logs.
#
# Optional: load this file when running the CLI outside the repo root:
#   OPENCLAW_ENV_FILE=/absolute/path/to/openclaw/.env openclaw …
# Or keep secrets in ~/openclaw/.env (same keys); the CLI also loads that path when cwd has no .env.

# --- Remote gateway (e.g. DigitalOcean droplet) ---
# Used for SSH and tunnel commands from your Mac; not read by OpenClaw automatically.
DROPLET_IP=YOUR_DROPLET_IP
# Optional: SSH via Tailscale (100.x or MagicDNS) instead of the public IP — set after UFW or cloud firewall restricts :22 to tailnet only (see docs/platforms/digitalocean.md).
# DROPLET_SSH_HOST=100.x.x.x
SSH_USER=root
# Optional SSH hardening (see docs/platforms/digitalocean.md → Further SSH hardening):
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_SSH_STRICT=1
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_KNOWN_HOSTS=/absolute/path/to/.droplet/known_hosts
# Optional: force passphrase prompt for an encrypted key (disables ssh-agent for this connection):
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_SSH_IDENTITY_AGENT_NONE=1
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_SSH_IDENTITY=/Users/you/.ssh/id_ed25519
# Optional: skip local sudo gate for droplet scripts and `openclaw … droplet` (automation only):
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_SUDO_GATE=0
# Optional: macOS only — completion chime (Funk / "funky" in System Settings): after `openclaw … droplet` SSH ends, and when a TUI run finishes (local Mac only; the droplet never triggers sound on your machine):
# OPENCLAW_COMPLETION_SOUND=0
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_COMPLETION_SOUND=0
# OPENCLAW_TUI_COMPLETION_SOUND=0
# OPENCLAW_COMPLETION_SOUND_NAME=funky
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_COMPLETION_SOUND_NAME=funky
# OPENCLAW_COMPLETION_SOUND_PATH=/System/Library/Sounds/Funk.aiff
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_COMPLETION_SOUND_PATH=/System/Library/Sounds/Funk.aiff
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_COMPLETION_SOUND_SUCCESS_ONLY=1
# Optional: `openclaw … droplet` SSH exit chime on macOS. Default skips chime when the remote command is `tui` (SSH stays open; use local `openclaw tui` with your gateway URL for a sound when each agent reply finishes). Set to 1 to play on SSH exit for remote tui too; 0 to never play on SSH exit.
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_SSH_EXIT_CHIME=1
# Optional: remote host for SSH `-L` when the gateway on the VPS does not listen on loopback (for example `gateway.bind: tailnet`). Set to the droplet Tailscale IPv4 (`tailscale ip -4` on the server). Default `127.0.0.1`. Also used by `./scripts/droplet-tunnel.sh`.
# OPENCLAW_DROPLET_SSH_FORWARD_HOST=100.x.x.x
# Optional: only if you use password auth (prefer SSH keys). If the value
# contains shell metacharacters like ( ) , { } # wrap the whole value in
# single quotes, e.g. SSH_KEY_PW='your-password-here'
# SSH_KEY_PW=

# --- OpenClaw runtime (optional overrides; defaults under $HOME/.openclaw) ---
# OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=$HOME/.openclaw
# OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=$HOME/.openclaw/openclaw.json

# --- Model providers (examples — use names your shell and tools expect) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Moonshot/Kimi (also forwarded to droplet gateway via sync; use *_DROPLET for droplet-only keys)
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# KIMI_API_KEY=

# Load before SSH:  set -a && source .env && set +a
# SSH (repo helpers always sudo-gate, then sudo -k on exit):
#   ./scripts/droplet-ssh.sh
#   ./scripts/droplet-tunnel.sh   # Control UI port forward to localhost:18789
#   ./scripts/verify-droplet-openclaw.sh   # remote `command -v` + `openclaw --version`
#   ./scripts/droplet-record-host-key.sh   # write .droplet/known_hosts for stricter SSH
# Run any CLI on the droplet (needs DROPLET_IP):  openclaw status droplet
# For `openclaw tui droplet` / gateway commands: set OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN (and password if used)
# in this file or ~/.openclaw/.env — the CLI forwards them to the remote non-login SSH session so
# the remote TUI can authenticate to the VPS gateway (same token the gateway expects).
# Optional if remote binary path/name differs (use absolute path if `openclaw` is not on non-login PATH):
# OPENCLAW_REMOTE_BIN=/usr/bin/openclaw
#
# Push model/provider secrets to a DigitalOcean droplet (encrypted over SSH):
#   ./scripts/sync-droplet-secrets.sh
# (On the droplet, that script sets OPENCLAW_AUTH_STORE_READONLY=1 for the gateway user unit.)
#
# Limits and mitigations (canonical scripts, sshd, drift, secrets): docs/platforms/digitalocean.md
